## Response Format

Return a single JSON object:

```json
{
  "summary": "Brief one-line summary of what this file does",
  "entities": [
    {
      "name": "EntityName",
      "entityType": "Class",
      "description": "What this entity does",
      "properties": {
        "package": "com.example",
        "visibility": "public"
      }
    }
  ],
  "relationships": [
    {
      "fromEntity": "EntityA",
      "toEntity": "EntityB",
      "relationType": "calls",
      "description": "EntityA invokes EntityB for processing",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "cobolReferences": [
    {
      "entityName": "JavaServiceClass",
      "targetName": "PROG001",
      "targetType": "Program",
      "referenceType": "wraps",
      "description": "Java service wraps calls to COBOL program PROG001"
    }
  ]
}
```

**Important:**
- Only extract entities that are genuinely meaningful — skip trivial imports, getters/setters, etc.
- The `properties` field on entities is optional and free-form — include any properties that seem important
- Be conservative with COBOL references — only include clear, confident matches
- If the file is empty or contains no meaningful content, return empty arrays

